rlm-wts

Fuzzy-pick a git worktree from the current repository and cd
into it, with Jira annotations on each line. Outside a git
repository, falls back to picking a multi-repo collection
directory from the current directory's family (see COLLECTION
MODE below).

Lists every worktree via `git worktree list`, then for each
worktree whose branch name contains a Jira-style key (regex
`[A-Z][A-Z0-9]+-[0-9]+`, e.g. DATA-1234, feature/DATA-9)
fetches `(Status) Summary` from Jira via the `acli` CLI in
parallel and shows it inline.

The fzf preview pane is the shared ~/bin/wt-preview script:
path, branch, Jira summary (clickable link), pull request,
created and updated times, and the list of files changed
against origin/<default-branch> with +adds/-dels per file.

Display rules:
  * $HOME is shortened to ~
  * the longest common path prefix across all worktrees is
    stripped

COLLECTION MODE

`rlm-pr-worktree`'s multi-repo mode turns a plain directory
holding several repositories (a "base" directory, such as
~/git/work/StorytelDataPlatform) into sibling "collection"
directories named <basename>_<YYYYMMDD>_<tail>, each holding
one worktree of every repository, all on a shared branch.

Run from the base directory *or* from any collection in the
family, rlm-wts lists the whole family newest-first and cds
into the one you pick. The preview pane is
~/bin/wt-collection-preview: the Jira summary (clickable link,
key taken from the directory name or, failing that, from a
member worktree's branch), the shared branch, created and
updated times, and a per-repository roll-up of changes.
Repositories that differ from their default branch are listed
with their changed files; the rest collapse onto a single
"unchanged:" line.

The family is found by truncating the current directory name at
the first "_" to get a stem, then globbing both <stem> and
<stem>_* next to it. Truncating is what lets the picker work
from inside a collection as well as from the base directory:
collections have no children of their own, so globbing the full
directory name would match nothing. The base directory itself is
included in the list, and the current directory is flagged
"<- here".

That matches the name rlm-pr-worktree generates by default, but
the name is editable when the worktree is created, so a renamed
collection will not be listed. A collection whose name is edited
to change the part before the first "_" lands in a different
family.

Rows are built from directory timestamps only; the per-repo git
diffs run lazily in the preview for the highlighted row, so the
picker opens immediately.

In a directory that is neither a git repository nor a base
directory containing repositories, rlm-wts does nothing.

Jira data is cached in ~/.cache/wts-jira/ as <KEY>.summary,
refreshed hourly by the picker and on a 3-day TTL by the
preview scripts. A 3-second watchdog kills any hung acli call
so the picker never freezes. If `acli` is not installed, the
function still works but without annotations.

Aliases: wts
